 ## Background
-SA3D was introduced as a method building upon the Segment Anything Model (SAM) [119] to advance 3D segmentation [S1]. It is part of a series of works leveraging 3DGS for semantic tasks, following methods like Feature 3DGS [53], SAGA [54], SAGD [55], and Gaussian Grouping [56] [S1].
+SA3D was introduced as a framework building upon SAM to advance 3D segmentation using radiance fields [S1]. It is part of a series of works leveraging 3DGS for semantic tasks, following methods like Feature 3DGS [53], SAGA [54], SAGD [55], and Gaussian Grouping [56] [S3].
 
